.TH tkuvalidate n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuvalidate
.PP
Inline validation feedback for input widgets. Attach a validator to an entry/combo/spinbox: on focus\-out (or on every key) the value is checked; invalid input gets a red foreground, the ttk \fBinvalid\fR state, and a \fBtkuballoon\fR message explaining why; valid input clears all that. The GUI companion to \fBtclutils::tuvalidate\fR (which supplies the predicates). Pure Tk + tclutils.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkuvalidate::attach $w $validator \
    ?-message s? ?-when focusout|key|both? ?-allowempty 0|1? \
    ?-getcmd cmd? ?-onvalid cmd? ?-oninvalid cmd?
::tkutils::tkuvalidate::check  $w        ;# validate now -> 0|1
::tkutils::tkuvalidate::valid  $w        ;# last result
::tkutils::tkuvalidate::clear  $w        ;# remove marking + detach
::tkutils::tkuvalidate::allValid {w ...} ;# re-check all; 1 only if every one valid
.CE
.PP
\fB$validator\fR is either a \fBtclutils::tuvalidate\fR predicate name (\fBemail url ipv4 port alpha alnum numeric integer\fR) or any command prefix to which the widget value is appended and that returns a boolean.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkuvalidate
tkuvalidate::attach .email email   -message "Enter a valid e-mail"
tkuvalidate::attach .age   integer -message "Digits only" -when key -allowempty 0
tkuvalidate::attach .user  [list apply {{v} {expr {[string length $v] >= 3}}}] \
    -message "At least 3 characters"
if {[tkuvalidate::allValid {.email .age .user}]} { save }
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
\fB\-allowempty 1\fR (default) leaves an empty field unmarked (optional fields); set \fB0\fR to require a value.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-getcmd\fR overrides how the value is read (default \fB[$w get]\fR); needed for text widgets, e.g. \fB\-getcmd {.notes get 1.0 end\-1c}\fR.
.IP \(bu
The message is shown via \fBtkutils::tkuballoon\fR (hover to read it); the red foreground is the immediate cue.
.IP \(bu
Errors carry \fB{TKUTILS TKUVALIDATE <REASON>}\fR (\fBNOWIDGET\fR, \fBOPTION\fR, \fBWHEN\fR, \fBNOENGINE\fR).
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tkuvalidate.tcl
.CE
